# Environment
.env
.env.*

# Auction state snapshots (runtime data). The glob covers the per-pool dirs
# `main._default_state_dir()` derives for an alternate FCHL_PLAYERS_CSV,
# e.g. data/state-players-23-converted/.
data/state*/

# Dropped-in copy of the pricer repo (source of model_params.json) — not part of this project
FCHL-auction-pricer/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Reference material dropped in data/ — league workbooks and the DobberHockey
# guides. Third-party publications, and four of them (17MB, two PDFs of 9.4MB
# and 6.0MB) were swept into a commit by `git add -A` on 2026-09-10, which is
# why this rule is by extension rather than by name.
#
# Since 2026-09-15 one of them IS an input: `convert_fchl_online.py` reads
# `data/dobberhockeydraftlist202627.xlsx` to build `data/players.csv`. It stays
# ignored anyway — it is a 1.3MB paid third-party file, the converter is run
# once a season by hand, and its OUTPUT is what the repo needs to carry. The
# league's own roster export beside it is committed, because that half is ours.
# So a `players.csv` rebuild needs the workbook fetched again; the converter's
# docstring says where from.
data/*.pdf
data/*.xlsx

# LibreOffice lock files (created while a data workbook is open)
.~lock.*#
